  "reason": "The strongest evidence is that RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 models reach ~0.65 validation accuracy, with transformer aggregation slightly ahead of avgpool, while image-only single-profile models are weak and ViT is marginally better than ResNet. The key uncertainty is whether image features add complementary signal to the already strong RNA multiprofile representation. config_038 tests this by adding an ImageNet ViT image branch to the best RNA multiprofile transformer setup using simple concat fusion, giving a direct comparison to the RNA-only baseline config_006. This is the best next use of budget because it exploits the strongest known direction while testing the most important unresolved design question: whether multimodal fusion improves performance over the best RNA-only model."
}

